# Quote depth carried from a host marker

## Root cause

The model's lone-plus scan recognizes a quote opened directly on a list marker, but it leaves the live quote depth at zero and misses quotes opened after nested list markers. A following line with fewer quote prefixes then raises that depth only to its visible prefix count. The scan treats a `+` after one prefix as missing the inner quote and refuses it, even when the marker line opened two quotes. The same quote run at document level keeps its inner depth and attaches.

## Change

Walk the marker chain on a host line to find its quote opener, then carry that opener's depth and source column into the scan's live quote path. A line with fewer explicit prefixes can then retain the already open inner quote through lazy continuation. Use that path when deciding whether a quoted `+` with a deeper quoted follower attaches.

## Scope

This tracks quote depth from any list marker that opens a quote chain. The decision follows container state and prefix depth, so it applies across marker spellings and nesting depths rather than matching the reported lines.
